   "core/anf_corrections.py - persist ANF preview edits keyed by PDF layout fingerprint.\n\nWhen the operator corrects an ANF entity/line field in the preview window\n(\"信息确认\" tab or the editable RawData grid), the correction is stored on disk\nkeyed by the source PDF's ``layout_fingerprint``. On the NEXT parse of the same\nPDF, :func:`apply_anf_corrections` replays the stored values so the operator does\nnot have to re-type them — the \"memory\" the ANF Special flow needs across cases.\n\nThe edits are **value overrides** (the same semantic as the standard confirm\ndialog's cleeds), NOT position relocations: where the value is read from in the\nPDF is still decided by the existing parser / recipe, only the extracted value is\noverwritten by the remembered correction.\n",
